Abigail — wife of Nabal, later David (1 Sam 25); David's sister, mother of Amasa (1 Chr 2:16–17)

Abijah — king of Judah, son of Rehoboam (1 Kings 15); son of Jeroboam I who died young (1 Kings 14); son of Samuel (1 Sam 8:2); Hezekiah's mother (2 Chr 29:1)

Abimelech — king of Gerar in Abraham's time (Gen 20); king of Gerar in Isaac's time (Gen 26); son of Gideon who seized kingship (Judges 9)

Abinadab — man in whose house the Ark rested (1 Sam 7:1); David's brother (1 Sam 16:8); Saul's son killed at Gilboa (1 Sam 31:2)

Ahaziah — king of Israel, son of Ahab (1 Kings 22); king of Judah, son of Jehoram (2 Kings 8)

Ahimelech — priest at Nob (1 Sam 21); Ahimelech the Hittite, one of David's men (1 Sam 26:6)

Ahinoam — Saul's wife (1 Sam 14:50); David's wife from Jezreel (1 Sam 25:43)

Amasa — Absalom's commander, later David's (2 Sam 17:25); an Ephraimite chief (2 Chr 28:12)

Amaziah — king of Judah (2 Kings 14); priest of Bethel under Jeroboam II (Amos 7:10)

Amram — father of Moses, Aaron, Miriam (Ex 6:18); a man with a foreign wife in Ezra's time (Ezra 10:34)

Asa — king of Judah (1 Kings 15); a Levite (1 Chr 9:16)

Azariah — alternate name of King Uzziah (2 Kings 15:1); Daniel's companion, Hebrew name of Abednego (Dan 1:7); a prophet, son of Oded (2 Chr 15:1); numerous priests

Baruch — Jeremiah's scribe (Jer 32); a wall-repairer under Nehemiah (Neh 3:20)

Boaz — Ruth's husband; also the name of a bronze pillar in Solomon's Temple (1 Kings 7:21) — not a person, but worth noting

Caleb — son of Jephunneh, the spy (Num 13); son of Hezron, in Judah's genealogy (1 Chr 2:18) — possibly the same figure by tradition, but listed separately in the text

Carmi — son of Reuben (Gen 46:9); father of Achan (Josh 7:1)

Deborah — Rebekah's nurse (Gen 35:8); the prophetess and judge (Judges 4–5)

Ehud — the judge who killed Eglon (Judges 3); a Benjamite in genealogies (1 Chr 7:10, 8:6)

Eleazar — son of Aaron, high priest; son of Abinadab, keeper of the Ark (1 Sam 7:1); one of David's mighty men (2 Sam 23:9)

Eliab — David's oldest brother (1 Sam 16:6); leader of Zebulun in the wilderness (Num 1:9); a Levite musician (1 Chr 15:18)

Eliakim — Hezekiah's palace administrator (2 Kings 18); King Josiah's son, renamed Jehoiakim (2 Kings 23:34)

Eliezer — Abraham's servant (Gen 15:2); Moses' son (Ex 18:4); a prophet, son of Dodavahu (2 Chr 20:37)

Eliphaz — Esau's son (Gen 36:4); Job's friend, "the Temanite" (Job 2:11)

Elkanah — Samuel's father (1 Sam 1); several Levites in genealogical lists (1 Chr 6, 15:23)

Elon — son of Zebulun (Gen 46:14); a judge of Israel (Judges 12:11); Esau's Hittite father-in-law (Gen 26:34)

Enoch/Hanoch — Cain's son (Gen 4:17); Seth's descendant who "walked with God" (Gen 5:21); Reuben's son (Gen 46:9)

Er — Judah's son (Gen 38); a descendant in 1 Chr 4:21

Gad — Jacob's son, tribal ancestor; the prophet/seer of David (1 Sam 22:5, 2 Sam 24)

Gedaliah — governor appointed after Jerusalem's fall (2 Kings 25); father of the prophet Zephaniah (Zeph 1:1); a musician (1 Chr 25:3)

Hananiah — a false prophet (Jer 28); Hebrew name of Shadrach (Dan 1:7); numerous priests/Levites

Hezron — son of Perez (Gen 46:12); son of Reuben (Gen 46:9)

Hilkiah — high priest under Josiah (2 Kings 22); Jeremiah's father (Jer 1:1); Eliakim's father (2 Kings 18:18)

Hosea/Hoshea — the prophet; the last king of Israel (2 Kings 17); Joshua's original name before Moses renamed him (Num 13:16)

Jair — conqueror of towns in Gilead (Num 32:41); a judge (Judges 10:3); Mordecai's father (Esther 2:5)

Jehoahaz — king of Judah, son of Josiah (also called Shallum); king of Israel, son of Jehu (2 Kings 13)

Jeremiah — the prophet; father of Josiah's wife Hamutal (2 Kings 23:31); several Gadite warriors who joined David (1 Chr 12); a Rechabite (Jer 35:3)

Joash/Jehoash — king of Judah; king of Israel; Gideon's father (Judges 6); Ahab's son (1 Kings 22:26)

Joel — the prophet; Samuel's son (1 Sam 8:2); an enormous number of Levites and tribal chiefs throughout Chronicles

Jonathan — Saul's son; Abiathar's son (2 Sam 15:27); one of David's mighty men (2 Sam 21:21); a scribe in whose house Jeremiah was imprisoned (Jer 37:15)

Joseph — Jacob's son; the spy from Issachar's tribe (Num 13:7); a Levite musician (1 Chr 25:2)

Josiah — king of Judah; a man in whose house Zechariah performed a symbolic act (Zech 6:10)

Judah — Jacob's son, tribal ancestor; a Levite in Ezra/Nehemiah (Ezra 3:9, Neh 12:8)

Kenaz — Esau's grandson, an Edomite chief (Gen 36:11); Othniel's father (Judges 1:13); Caleb's grandson (1 Chr 4:15)

Korah — Esau's son (Gen 36:5); the Levite rebel (Num 16); a son of Hebron (1 Chr 2:43)

Manasseh — Joseph's son, tribal ancestor (Gen 41:51); king of Judah (2 Kings 21); two men with foreign wives in Ezra 10:30, 33

Mephibosheth — Jonathan's son (2 Sam 4:4); Saul's son by Rizpah (2 Sam 21:8)

Micah — the man with the idol shrine in Ephraim (Judges 17–18); the prophet (Book of Micah). Note: the "Micaiah" who confronted Ahab in 1 Kings 22 is a related but technically distinct Hebrew name (Michaiah).

Nadab — Aaron's son (Lev 10); king of Israel, son of Jeroboam (1 Kings 15); a descendant of Jerahmeel (1 Chr 2:28)

Nathan — the prophet (2 Sam 7, 12); David's son (2 Sam 5:14); father of one of David's mighty men (2 Sam 23:36)

Obadiah — the prophet; Ahab's steward who hid 100 prophets (1 Kings 18); an official under Josiah (2 Chr 34:12)

Obed — son of Boaz and Ruth, David's grandfather (Ruth 4:17); one of David's mighty men (1 Chr 11:47); a gatekeeper (1 Chr 26:7)

Phinehas — Aaron's zealous grandson (Num 25); Eli's wicked son (1 Sam 1:3)

Reuel — alternate name for Moses' father-in-law Jethro (Ex 2:18); Esau's son (Gen 36:4)

Saul/Shaul — Israel's first king; an Edomite king (Gen 36:37); Simeon's son (Gen 46:10)

Shallum — king of Israel (2 Kings 15:10); Huldah the prophetess's husband (2 Kings 22:14); alternate name for King Jehoahaz (Jer 22:11)

Shammah — David's brother (1 Sam 16:9); one of David's mighty men (2 Sam 23:11); an Edomite chief (Gen 36:13)

Shelah — Judah's son (Gen 38:5); an ancestor in the line from Noah to Abraham (Gen 11:12–15)

Shimei — the man who cursed David (2 Sam 16); a Levite, Gershon's son (Ex 6:17); Solomon's officer in Benjamin (1 Kings 4:18); a descendant of David (1 Chr 3:19)

Tamar — Judah's daughter-in-law (Gen 38); David's daughter, Absalom's sister (2 Sam 13); Absalom's daughter (2 Sam 14:27)

Tola — Issachar's son (Gen 46:13); a judge (Judges 10:1)

Uriah — the Hittite, Bathsheba's husband (2 Sam 11); a priest under Ahaz (2 Kings 16:10); a prophet killed by Jehoiakim (Jer 26:20)

Uzziah — king of Judah (also called Azariah); one of David's mighty men (1 Chr 11:44); a priest in Ezra (Ezra 10:21)

Zechariah — the single most reused name in Tanach, worn by upwards of 25–30 distinct figures. Most notable: the prophet (Book of Zechariah); the king of Israel, Jehu's son (2 Kings 14–15); the priest son of Jehoiada, stoned in the Temple court (2 Chr 24:20–22); Hezekiah's grandfather (2 Kings 18:2)

Zedekiah — the last king of Judah (also called Mattaniah); a false prophet who told Ahab to attack Ramoth-gilead (1 Kings 22:11); another false prophet condemned by Jeremiah (Jer 29:21–22)

Zerah — Judah's son, Perez's twin (Gen 38:30); an Edomite chief (Gen 36:13); the Cushite king defeated by Asa (2 Chr 14:9)

Zimri — the Simeonite prince killed by Phinehas (Num 25:14); king of Israel who reigned seven days (1 Kings 16)